{"summary":"The task 'muse-acp-tools' expands the Muse ACP agent implementation so that Muse can act as a full coding agent in BB chats, executing local tools (read_file, write_file, edit_file, list_dir, grep, bash) in the session workspace directory via a multi-round tool loop. The design specified in .agents/plans/muse-agent.md relies on a text-based protocol because Muse cannot call tools natively. In this protocol, Muse ends tool-calling turns with a fenced ```muse-tool {"tool": "<name>", "args": {...}} ``` block. muse-acp parses the last block of the reply, sends ACP session/update tool_call and tool_call_update notifications to BB, streams any preceding text as thought chunks (agent_thought_chunk), executes the tool, and feeds the formatted tool result back to the same Muse chat as 'TOOL RESULT <name> (ok|error):\n<output>'. When Muse responds without a tool block, the reply is treated as the final message and streamed as agent_message_chunk with stopReason 'end_turn'.

Currently, bin/muse-acp.mjs implements an ACP server over stdio handling JSON-RPC methods (initialize, session/new, session/set_model, session/prompt, session/close, and session/cancel notification). In session/prompt, it acquires an account lock, opens a driver (real or fake), calls driver.send once, and streams deltas directly to BB as agent_message_chunk. It does not parse tool blocks, does not maintain a tool loop, does not store session cwd or clientCapabilities from initialize/session/new, and does not handle two-way ACP client requests (such as fs/read_text_file and fs/write_text_file). Furthermore, openFakeSession in bin/muse-acp.mjs currently only returns hardcoded 'PONG' responses and does not support the planned MUSE_BRIDGE_FAKE_SCRIPT or MUSE_BRIDGE_FAKE_SENT environments needed for testing tool interactions.

Key contractual constraints and invariants include: (1) all file operations must resolve within the session cwd, refusing paths outside cwd; (2) raw muse-tool blocks must never reach agent_message_chunk; (3) when client capabilities announce fs.readTextFile / fs.writeTextFile, file reads and writes must be delegated to ACP client requests (fs/read_text_file and fs/write_text_file with absolute paths) so BB tracks file changes; (4) the tool loop must stop at MUSE_MAX_TOOL_ROUNDS (default 60) with an explanatory message; (5) session/cancel must stop the loop between rounds; (6) invalid JSON or unknown tool calls must return structured error results to Muse; and (7) existing tests in tests/acp*.test.mjs must continue to pass alongside the new tests/acp-tools.test.mjs.","keyFacts":[".agents/plans/muse-agent.md states BB provides ACP client capabilities including fs.readTextFile: true, fs.writeTextFile: true, and terminal: false during initialize.","The first message of a Muse chat must include a short intro (< 8 KB) defining the agent role, cwd, tool protocol, tool list, tool_schema, and skill discovery (.agents/plans/muse-agent.md).","Muse calls tools by ending its reply with a fenced block: ```muse-tool\n{"tool":"<name>","args":{...}}\n``` (.agents/plans/muse-agent.md).","muse-acp must parse the last muse-tool block of a reply, emitting an in_progress tool_call followed by a completed or failed tool_call_update capped at ~20 KB (.agents/plans/muse-agent.md).","Text preceding a muse-tool block streams to BB as agent_thought_chunk, while raw muse-tool blocks must never stream to agent_message_chunk (.agents/plans/muse-agent.md and task contract).","Tool execution results are returned to the Muse chat as 'TOOL RESULT <name> (ok|error):\n<output>' (.agents/plans/muse-agent.md).","A reply without a muse-tool block represents the final answer, streamed to BB as agent_message_chunk with stopReason end_turn (.agents/plans/muse-agent.md).","The tool loop is capped at MUSE_MAX_TOOL_ROUNDS (default 60) per prompt, terminating with an error message if exceeded, and stops between rounds on session/cancel (.agents/plans/muse-agent.md).","Local tools to support are read_file, write_file, edit_file (exact, unique match), list_dir, grep, and bash (runs in session cwd via /bin/bash -lc, default timeout 120s, max 600s, capped output) (.agents/plans/muse-agent.md).","File paths outside session cwd must be refused (.agents/plans/muse-agent.md and task contract).","When the ACP client announces fs.readTextFile / fs.writeTextFile, file operations must use ACP client requests fs/read_text_file and fs/write_text_file with absolute paths (.agents/plans/muse-agent.md).","Fake mode for tests must support MUSE_BRIDGE_FAKE_SCRIPT (JSON array of replies in order) and MUSE_BRIDGE_FAKE_SENT (appending {"text": ...} per sent message) (.agents/plans/muse-agent.md).","bin/muse-acp.mjs currently receives initialize and session/new but does not store clientCapabilities or session cwd.","bin/muse-acp.mjs currently streams all onDelta chunks directly to agent_message_chunk without thought buffering or tool block filtering.","bin/muse-acp.mjs only handles incoming client requests and notifications on stdin; it lacks a pending-request map to receive responses for outgoing ACP client requests like fs/write_text_file.","openFakeSession in bin/muse-acp.mjs currently generates fixed 'PONG' responses without reading MUSE_BRIDGE_FAKE_SCRIPT or writing MUSE_BRIDGE_FAKE_SENT.","bridge/acp-prompt.mjs strips BB system instructions (<system_instructions> and <system-reminder>) from incoming prompts.","Existing tests in tests/acp.test.mjs verify initialize, session/new, session/set_model, and session persistence across multiple prompts via accounts.json and sessions.json."],"openQuestions":["How will outgoing JSON-RPC requests (e.g. fs/read_text_file, fs/write_text_file) sent to stdout match incoming JSON-RPC responses on stdin in bin/muse-acp.mjs, given the current line reader only processes messages with a 'method' property?","How should onDelta streaming distinguish thoughts from muse-tool blocks in real time before the full block boundary is received, to prevent raw muse-tool text from leaking to agent_message_chunk?","What exact properties and structure are expected in the tool_call and tool_call_update payloads (e.g., tool call ID generation, title format, kind categorization, and content structure)?","What are the contents and requirements of the other existing test files mentioned in owns_paths (tests/acp-cancel.test.mjs and tests/acp-pending.test.mjs), which were not included in the excerpts?","Does the initial intro message explaining the tool protocol and cwd need to be sent on every session/prompt or only on the first prompt of a new Muse chat session?","What specific output length limit applies to bash tool execution output before it is truncated?"]}
